Here is the full audit of `ProductCatalogTests.cs`.

---

## Summary

**10 tests analyzed · 8 Critical · 2 Medium · 0 Low**

This suite is a textbook example of **coverage-touching**: every public method on `ProductCatalog` is called exactly once, but almost nothing is actually verified. The 95% coverage number is meaningless — these tests would still pass if every method silently returned garbage or corrupted data.

---

## 🔴 Critical — Tests giving false confidence

### 1. Coverage-touching pattern (systemic)

All 10 tests follow a mechanical "call every method" pattern with zero or trivial assertions. This is the single root cause of your production bugs — the suite inflates coverage without verifying behavior.

### 2. No assertions (5 tests)

| Line | Method | Problem |
|------|--------|---------|
| 17 | `AddProduct_Works` | Calls `AddProduct`, never checks the product was stored |
| 33 | `UpdatePrice_Works` | Calls `UpdatePrice`, never checks the price changed |
| 39 | `RemoveProduct_Works` | Calls `RemoveProduct`, never checks the product is gone |
| 63 | `GetProductCount_Works` | Captures `count` in a local variable, never asserts it |
| 68 | `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` | Applies discount, never checks resulting prices |

**Fix** — each test must assert the observable outcome. Examples:

```csharp
// AddProduct_Works → AddProduct_StoresProduct
[TestMethod]
public void AddProduct_StoresProduct()
{
    var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
    _catalog.AddProduct(product);

    var stored = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual(product, stored);
}

// UpdatePrice_Works → UpdatePrice_ChangesPrice
[TestMethod]
public void UpdatePrice_ChangesPrice()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);

    var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated!.Price);
}

// RemoveProduct_Works → RemoveProduct_MakesProductUnfindable
[TestMethod]
public void RemoveProduct_MakesProductUnfindable()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");

    Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
}

// GetProductCount_Works → GetProductCount_ReturnsCorrectCount
[TestMethod]
public void GetProductCount_ReturnsCorrectCount()
{
    Assert.AreEqual(0, _catalog.GetProductCount());
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
